              "content": "Describing Motion Around Us"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.856,
            0.018,
            0.953,
            0.088
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "N 69"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.087,
            0.775,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. A girl is riding her scooter and finds that its speedometer reading is constant. Is it possible for her scooter to be accelerating and if so, how?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.125,
            0.775,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A car starts from rest and its velocity reaches "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 4 \\; \\mathrm { m \\; s ^ { - 1 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in 6 s. Find the average acceleration and the distance travelled in these 6 s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.163,
            0.775,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. A motorbike moving with initial velocity 28 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "S ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and constant acceleration stops after travelling 98 m. Find the acceleration of the motorbike and the time taken to come to a stop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.219,
            0.775,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Fig. 4.27 shows a position-time graph of two objects A and B that are moving along the parallel tracks in the same direction. Do objects A and B ever have equal velocity? Justify your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.282,
            0.399,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.155,
                0.282,
                0.399,
                0.472
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_21_chart_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "chart_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.256,
                0.473,
                0.322,
                0.489
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 4.27"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "chart",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.485,
            0.282,
            0.738,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "chart_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.485,
                0.282,
                0.738,
                0.489
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_21_chart_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.495,
            0.775,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. A graph in Fig. 4.28 shows the change in position with time for two objects A and B moving in a straight line from 0 to 10 seconds. Choose the correct option(s)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.547,
            0.774,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The average velocity of both over the 10 s time interval is equal since they have the same initial and final positions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.583,
            0.774,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The average speeds of both over the 10 s time interval are equal since both cover equal distance in equal time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.617,
            0.775,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) The average speed of A over the 10 s time interval is lower than that of B since it covers a shorter distance than B in 10 seconds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.651,
            0.775,
            0.686
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iv) The average speed of A over the 10 s time interval is greater than that of B since B’s speed is lower than A’s in some segments."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.798,
            0.542,
            0.95,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.798,
                0.542,
                0.95,
                0.722
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_21_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.689,
            0.776,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. A truck driver driving at the speed of 54 km "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { h } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " notices a road sign with a speed limit of 40 km "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { h } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (Fig. 4.29) for trucks. He slows down to 36 km "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { h } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in 36 s. What was the distance travelled by him during this time? Assume the acceleration to be constant while slowing down."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.842,
            0.733,
            0.907,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 4.29"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.761,
            0.775,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly to 20 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in 5 seconds. It then travels at 20 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for 10 seconds and finally applies the brake (with uniform acceleration) to stop in 6 seconds. Find the total distance travelled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.833,
            0.776,
            0.921
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. A bus is travelling at 36 km "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { h } ^ { - 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " when the driver sees an obstacle 30 m ahead. The driver takes 0.5 seconds to react before pressing the brake. Once the brake is applied, the velocity of the bus reduces with constant acceleration of 2.5 m "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbb { S } ^ { - 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Will the bus be able to stop before reaching the obstacle?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
